# V1 scope (locked)

Product: Denmark tenant/landlord laundry booking. Local-first. No Azure deploy until landlord panel basics exist. Free-tier when deploy later.

## In scope

1. Finish Mongo → Postgres cutover (auth/bookings/tenants must not depend on Mongo).
2. Refresh tokens persisted in Postgres; verify cookie auth (HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite) during that work.
3. Book + cancel laundry slots end-to-end on Postgres.
4. No double booking: DB uniqueness/concurrency on slot + tests.
5. Tenant isolation: shared DB + tenant/building key on rows + enforced filters + integration tests. No separate-schema / RLS in V1.
6. Landlord creates tenant accounts (option A) — allowlist only; no open self-serve signup for booking users.
7. BuildingSettings foundation: slot length, max bookings/week (even if UI is minimal).
8. API + Web versioning basics (not Danish i18n yet).
9. Tests on auth + booking isolation paths.
10. Landlord panel only as far as: manage tenants + see bookings.

## Out of scope (V2+)

Danish i18n, notice board, slot trading, Face ID, photo fault reports, varmemester forward, CSV/PDF regnskab, App Insights/alerts, IP banlists, schema-per-tenant, RLS, cold-start ping cron, payment/Bogføringslov.

## Defaults when unsure

- Ship simplest correct isolation and invite model.
- Attach learning to a shippable outcome (no orphan “learn YAML” tickets).
- Update `ROADMAP.md` checkboxes when a milestone lands — do not expand V1 without Sten explicitly unlocking scope.
